                "text": "ISSUE_KIND: road_damage\nISSUE: Sinkhole and severe pavement failure in the roadway\nDETAILS: The photo shows a large sinkhole with significant pavement collapse extending across the street next to a storm drain inlet structure, exposing eroded soil underneath and holding a wooden safety barricade/signpost. The user note states that the road caved in next to the storm drain about 4 feet across.\nORGANIZATION: Prince George's County Department of Public Works and Transportation\nDEPARTMENT: Office of Highway Maintenance\nWHY: Tecumseh Street in Adelphi is located in unincorporated Prince George's County, Maryland. The Prince George's County Department of Public Works and Transportation (Office of Highway Maintenance) maintains county-owned residential roads and handles pavement failure and sinkhole repairs.\nCOVERAGE_QUOTE: \"As part of the Prince George's County Roadway Preservation Program, maintenance includes the repair of sinkholes and potholes, shoulder repair, removal and replacement of concrete curb and gutter, sidewalks, driveway aprons, the installation of underdrains, the installation and/or upgrade of handicapped access ramps per ADA standards and the repair/resurfacing of the roadway pavement.\"\nCOVERAGE_URL: https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/departments-offices/public-works-transportation/about-dpwt/office-highway-maintenance\nREPORTING_URL: https://www.pgc311.com\nOFFICIAL_WEBSITE: https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/departments-offices/public-works-transportation\nEMAIL: unknown\nPHONE: 311 | https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/departments-offices/public-works-transportation/report-public-works-problem/potholes\nPHOTO_LOOKS_DAYTIME: yes\nNOTE_SAYS_LIGHT_OUT: no\nSOURCES:\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/departments-offices/public-works-transportation/about-dpwt/office-highway-maintenance\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/departments-offices/public-works-transportation/report-public-works-problem/potholes\nh